<p>Living in Meridianville means living with trees. Lots of trees. Those beautiful pines, oaks, and sweet gums that make the area so appealing also dump an incredible amount of debris into your gutters — pine needles year-round, leaves every fall, seed pods and twigs throughout the year.</p>

<p>Without protection, Meridianville homeowners find themselves cleaning gutters 3-4 times a year (or paying someone else to do it). Each cleaning runs $150-200+, and that's assuming you can find someone willing to make the drive out. Over a few years, those costs add up to more than a quality gutter guard system that solves the problem permanently.</p>

<p>When gutters clog in Meridianville, the consequences are real. Water overflows, runs down your siding, and on sloped lots, heads straight for your foundation. Gutter guards prevent all of this — keeping debris out while letting rainwater flow through.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Gutter guards are protective covers or screens that fit over or inside your gutters, allowing water to enter while blocking leaves, pine needles, twigs, and other debris. They work by creating a barrier that debris can't penetrate while still allowing rainwater to flow through.</p>

<p>Different types work better for different debris. Micro-mesh guards excel at blocking fine debris like pine needles. Screen guards handle larger leaves effectively. Solid covers use surface tension to pull water in while debris slides off.</p>

<p>For most Meridianville homes with heavy pine and hardwood coverage, we typically recommend micro-mesh guards. But we'll assess your specific situation and recommend the best solution during your free estimate.</p>
{% endset %}

